this silently reverts a9c551e5e38f

potential fix? (AI suggestion idk, seems good though):


"kill the dead marktree seek (restores what a9c551e5e38f bought)":

```diff
/// Like init_charsize_arg(), for a caller that measures the text after `cur` but not the inline
/// virtual text at `cur` itself (see CharsizeArg.skip_cur_text). That mode never reads `iter`, so
/// skip seeding it; only the row is needed, for the 'linebreak' lookahead's own iterator.
CSType init_charsize_arg_skip_cur_text(CharsizeArg *csarg, win_T *wp, linenr_T lnum, char *line)
{
  CSType cstype = init_charsize_arg(csarg, wp, 0, line);
  csarg->skip_cur_text = true;
  if (lnum > 0) {
    csarg->virt_row = lnum - 1;
    cstype = kCharsizeRegular;
  }
  return cstype;
}
-          CSType cstype = init_charsize_arg(&csarg, wp, lnum, line);
-          csarg.skip_cur_text = true;
+          CSType cstype = init_charsize_arg_skip_cur_text(&csarg, wp, lnum, line);
```

