comment_data.body:
> TAB inside the measured word gets the wrong padding. vcol2 += win_chartabsize(wp, s, vcol2) + virt_width; evaluates the tab stop before adding the virt width, so a tab drawn after inline text is off by up to ts-1.

suggestion


```diff
-    vcol2 += win_chartabsize(wp, s, vcol2) + virt_width;
+    // Add the virtual text first: it is drawn in front of the character, so a TAB's stop is
+    // computed at the shifted column (the main loop recomputes tab_size for the same reason).
+    vcol2 += virt_width;
+    vcol2 += win_chartabsize(wp, s, vcol2);
```

